# Installed first in GuardDog's virtualenv: pip itself, and the build dependencies of the sdists
# without a wheel for Alpaquita's Python (pygit2, yara-python). Those are built with
# --no-build-isolation, so their build dependencies come from this hash-checked lock, not from an
# unverified download. cffi must be there: without it pygit2 builds silently without its _libgit2
# extension. Constrained to the runtime lock, so shared packages keep the same version.
# Locked with hashes in guarddog-build-requirements.txt.
#
# Regenerate both locks (after changing a version here or in guarddog-requirements.in, or to pick
# up fixes) in the image's own Python: run from the repository root, with the Alpaquita digest of
# the Dockerfile,
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD/docker:/w" -w /w bellsoft/alpaquita-linux-base:stream-glibc@sha256:<digest> sh -c '
#     apk add --no-cache python3 py3-pip && python3 -m venv /v && /v/bin/pip install pip-tools &&
#     /v/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras --upgrade guarddog-requirements.in &&
#     /v/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras --upgrade guarddog-build-requirements.in'
# then check the diff and rebuild the image (docker build .).
-c guarddog-requirements.txt
pip==26.2.2
setuptools
wheel
cffi
